<section id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title" class="relative scroll-mt-20 py-12 md:py-20">
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] pr-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-right))] pl-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-left))]">
<header class="mb-10 md:mb-12 mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
<h2 id="problem-title" class="text-section mb-0 text-balance">Health factors fall while you sleep</h2>
</header>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-[72ch]">
<div class="grid gap-4">
<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">Aave shows your health factor in its app and warns you inside its transaction screens, but as of October 2026 it doesn&#x27;t send alerts. ETH drops overnight, interest keeps accruing on your debt, or a governance update trims a liquidation threshold, and nothing messages you about any of it.</p>
<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">On Aave&#x27;s governance forum, one borrower describes<!-- --> <a href="https://governance.aave.com/t/unexpected-or-poorly-executed-settlement-by-the-system/21120" rel="noopener noreferrer">checking in the morning to find the position liquidated again</a>; another,<!-- --> <a href="https://governance.aave.com/t/repeatedly-failed-repayment-attempts-leading-to-liquidation/20379" rel="noopener noreferrer">an hour of repay transactions that kept failing until the position was liquidated</a>. On the Polygon forum in 2021, before Aave V3, one borrower<!-- --> <a href="https://forum.polygon.technology/t/liquidation-on-polygon-aave-json-error/8067" rel="noopener noreferrer">tried to repay at a health factor of 1.01</a> and was liquidated before the transaction went through.</p>
<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">By the time you look, a liquidator may have taken collateral worth the repaid debt plus a bonus: 5% on WETH in the Ethereum Core market as of October 2026.<!-- --> <a href="/blog/how-aave-liquidation-works">What happens in an Aave liquidation</a> <!-- -->walks through the rules.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] pr-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-right))] pl-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-left))]">
<div aria-hidden="true" class="divider-brand print:hidden">
</div>
</div>
<section id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-it-works-title" class="relative scroll-mt-20 py-12 md:py-20">
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] pr-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-right))] pl-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-left))]">
<header class="mb-10 md:mb-12 mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
<h2 id="how-it-works-title" class="text-section mb-0 text-balance">How it works, in 4 steps</h2>
</header>
<div>
<ol class="m-0 grid list-none gap-6 p-0 lg:grid-cols-2">
<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 m-0 grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 sm:flex sm:items-start sm:gap-5">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand-plum text-base font-bold text-brand-white sm:size-12 sm:text-lg dark:outline dark:outline-border">1</span>
<div class="contents sm:block sm:min-w-0 sm:pt-1">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">
<span class="sr-only">1.</span> Connect the wallet you borrow with (read-only, free)</h3>
<p class="col-span-2 m-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:mt-2 md:text-base">The dashboard shows that wallet&#x27;s collateral, debt and health factor on Aave V3 on all 7 networks, and in every Aave V4 Spoke where the wallet has collateral or debt. Tokenping watches the wallet you connect; you can&#x27;t add another address.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 m-0 grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 sm:flex sm:items-start sm:gap-5">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand-plum text-base font-bold text-brand-white sm:size-12 sm:text-lg dark:outline dark:outline-border">2</span>
<div class="contents sm:block sm:min-w-0 sm:pt-1">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">
<span class="sr-only">2.</span> Unlock alerts: 3 USDC for 30 days, paid on Arbitrum One (approve, then pay)</h3>
<p class="col-span-2 m-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:mt-2 md:text-base">Two wallet transactions: an approval for exactly the price, never an unlimited one, then the payment. Nothing renews automatically.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 m-0 grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 sm:flex sm:items-start sm:gap-5">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand-plum text-base font-bold text-brand-white sm:size-12 sm:text-lg dark:outline dark:outline-border">3</span>
<div class="contents sm:block sm:min-w-0 sm:pt-1">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">
<span class="sr-only">3.</span> Pick a threshold and your channels for each market (1.1 to 10, default 1.5)</h3>
<p class="col-span-2 m-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:mt-2 md:text-base">Each Aave V3 network and each Aave V4 Spoke is a separate alert, because V4 keeps a separate position with its own health factor in every Spoke. Send it to Signal or email, or to more than one.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 m-0 grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 sm:flex sm:items-start sm:gap-5">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand-plum text-base font-bold text-brand-white sm:size-12 sm:text-lg dark:outline dark:outline-border">4</span>
<div class="contents sm:block sm:min-w-0 sm:pt-1">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">
<span class="sr-only">4.</span> We check every 5 minutes and message you while you&#x27;re below it</h3>
<p class="col-span-2 m-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:mt-2 md:text-base">Every check sends one message per channel until your health factor is back at or above your threshold, or you delete the alert. A fast drop can cross 1.0 between two checks.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] pr-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-right))] pl-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-left))]">
<div aria-hidden="true" class="divider-brand print:hidden">
</div>
</div>
<section id="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-title" class="relative scroll-mt-20 py-12 md:py-20">
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] pr-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-right))] pl-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-left))]">
<header class="mb-10 md:mb-12 mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
<h2 id="pricing-title" class="text-section mb-0 text-balance">Pricing</h2>
</header>
<div>
<div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-center lg:gap-x-12">
<dl class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 m-0 flex flex-col py-2 md:py-3 lg:col-span-7">
<div class="flex flex-col gap-0.5 border-t border-border py-3 first:border-t-0 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6">
<dt class="text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground sm:w-28 sm:shrink-0">Dashboard</dt>
<dd class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">Free</dd>
</div>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-0.5 border-t border-border py-3 first:border-t-0 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6">
<dt class="text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground sm:w-28 sm:shrink-0">Alerts</dt>
<dd class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">3 USDC per 30 days</dd>
</div>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-0.5 border-t border-border py-3 first:border-t-0 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6">
<dt class="text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground sm:w-28 sm:shrink-0">Renewal</dt>
<dd class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">None automatic: you pay again when you want more time</dd>
</div>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-0.5 border-t border-border py-3 first:border-t-0 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-6">
<dt class="text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground sm:w-28 sm:shrink-0">Payment</dt>
<dd class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">USDC on Arbitrum One, from your wallet (approve, then pay)</dd>
</div>
</dl>
<div class="mt-8 flex flex-col items-center gap-3 lg:col-span-5 lg:mt-0 lg:items-start">
<p class="m-0 text-center text-sm text-muted-foreground lg:text-left">The price is read from the payment contract and refreshed hourly.</p>
<a class="btn gap-2 font-medium whitespace-nowrap transition-[color,background-color,border-color,box-shadow,filter,translate] duration-200 ease-[ease] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring active:not-aria-[haspopup]:translate-y-px disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 aria-disabled:pointer-events-none not-aria-busy:aria-disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 btn-neutral border-transparent hover:bg-inverse/90 motion-safe:hover:-translate-y-0.5 disabled:bg-inverse! disabled:text-inverse-foreground btn-lg px-6 text-base [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-5 w-full max-w-sm sm:w-auto" href="/aave">Set up alerts: 3 USDC for 30 days</a>
<p class="m-0 text-center text-sm text-muted-foreground lg:text-left">Paid in USDC on Arbitrum One. No auto-renew.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title" class="relative scroll-mt-20 py-12 md:py-20 bg-linear-to-b from-background via-accent/60 to-background dark:via-accent/40">
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] pr-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-right))] pl-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-left))]">
<header class="mb-10 md:mb-12 mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
<h2 id="questions-title" class="text-section mb-0 text-balance">Questions to ask before you connect a wallet</h2>
</header>
<div>
<div class="lg:columns-2 lg:gap-x-4">
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 mb-3 break-inside-avoid lg:mb-4">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">Can Tokenping touch my funds?</h3>
<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base md:leading-[1.7]">No. Tokenping reads your positions and health factor with read-only calls and never asks for an approval or a signature on Aave. The only wallet transactions are the payment for alerts: an approval for exactly the price, never an unlimited one, then the payment, both on <!-- -->Arbitrum One<!-- -->. The payment contract<!-- --> <!-- -->is <a href="https://repo.sourcify.dev/42161/0x79872d7529cfE1c062838fACDA004Ce4BFB16553" rel="noopener noreferrer">verified on Sourcify</a> and its<!-- --> <a href="https://github.com/romispectrum/tokenping" rel="noopener noreferrer">source code is public on GitHub</a>. It is upgradeable and controlled by the Tokenping team&#x27;s wallet, which can change the price, pause payments, withdraw what was paid and upgrade the contract.</p>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 mb-3 break-inside-avoid lg:mb-4">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">What do you store?</h3>
<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base md:leading-[1.7]">Your wallet address, the networks, Aave V4 Spokes and thresholds you set, the channels you picked, and your email address and/or Signal username<!-- -->. If you answer the optional &quot;How did you hear about Tokenping?&quot; question, that answer too. Tokenping keeps no health factor history and no log of sent alerts, and this site runs no analytics. To read your positions, your wallet address is sent to RPC providers. Payments are public on <!-- -->Arbitrum One<!-- -->: anyone can see the paying address, the amount and the new expiry. Until the app checks wallet signatures, anyone who knows your wallet address can look up the contact details saved for it. The <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> explains this and lists every service that handles your data.</p>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 mb-3 break-inside-avoid lg:mb-4">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">What does it cost, and is there a catch?</h3>
<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base md:leading-[1.7]">The dashboard is free. Alerts cost <!-- -->3 USDC per 30 days<!-- -->, paid in native USDC on <!-- -->Arbitrum One<!-- --> even if your position is on another network, so you need USDC and a little ETH for gas there. It takes two transactions: approve, then pay. Nothing renews automatically, and paying again extends your access from its current end date. The contract has no refund function.</p>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 mb-3 break-inside-avoid lg:mb-4">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">What if an alert doesn&#x27;t arrive?</h3>
<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base md:leading-[1.7]">Tokenping checks every <!-- -->5<!-- --> minutes. A failed check or message is logged, and the next check tries again while your health factor is still below your threshold. Delivery depends on third parties (Resend for email, a Signal relay,<!-- --> public RPC nodes and Vercel&#x27;s scheduler), and Tokenping is in beta with no uptime guarantee. A fast crash can cross 1.0 between two checks. So pick two channels, set your threshold with room to act, and don&#x27;t make an alert your only safeguard.</p>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 mb-3 break-inside-avoid lg:mb-4">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">Is my position supported?</h3>
<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base md:leading-[1.7]">Aave V3 on Ethereum (Core market), Polygon, Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Avalanche and Gnosis. Aave V4 in every Spoke on Ethereum, Avalanche, Arc and Base: 20 Spokes, taken from Aave&#x27;s V4 API on 16 October 2026. Not supported: the other Aave V3 markets on Ethereum (Prime/Lido, EtherFi, Horizon), other Aave networks and other protocols. You get one alert per V3 network and one per V4 Spoke, for the wallet you connect. The dashboard lists a V4 Spoke once the wallet has collateral or debt in it, or an alert saved for it.</p>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 mb-3 break-inside-avoid lg:mb-4">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">How often will I be alerted, and how do I stop it?</h3>
<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base md:leading-[1.7]">Every <!-- -->5<!-- --> minutes on each channel you picked, for as long as your health factor is below your threshold. Alerts stop when it is back at or above your threshold, or when you delete the alert, which needs active access. If your access has expired, message us on<!-- --> <a href="https://x.com/tokenping" rel="noopener noreferrer">X</a> or in our<!-- --> <a href="https://t.me/tokenping_xyz" rel="noopener noreferrer">Telegram community</a> and we&#x27;ll delete it.<!-- --> There is no snooze, no &quot;recovered&quot; message and no unsubscribe link in the emails yet.</p>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 mb-3 break-inside-avoid lg:mb-4">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">Can I watch a wallet I don&#x27;t connect, or several wallets?</h3>
<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base md:leading-[1.7]">Not today. Tokenping watches the wallet you connect, and access is per paying wallet.</p>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-card md:p-7 mb-3 break-inside-avoid lg:mb-4">
<h3 class="m-0 text-lg leading-snug font-medium">Other tools are free. Why pay?</h3>
<p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base md:leading-[1.7]">If a Telegram bot or a mobile app works for you and you&#x27;d rather paste any address than connect a wallet, free tools exist<!-- -->:<!-- --> <a href="/blog/aave-liquidation-alert-tools">our comparison of Aave liquidation alert tools</a> <!-- -->covers them, including where they beat Tokenping<!-- -->. Tokenping is for people who want the alert on Signal or email, including for positions on Gnosis and Optimism.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title" class="relative scroll-mt-20 py-12 md:py-20">
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] pr-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-right))] pl-[max(1.25rem,env(safe-area-inset-left))]">
<header class="mb-10 md:mb-12 mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
<h2 id="limits-title" class="text-section mb-0 text-balance">Limits, stated plainly</h2>
</header>
<div>
<ul class="m-0 list-disc pl-6 marker:text-muted-foreground lg:columns-2 lg:gap-x-12">
<li class="mb-3 break-inside-avoid leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">Aave V3 on 7 networks, and on Ethereum only the Core market. Aave V4 in every Spoke on Ethereum, Avalanche, Arc and Base. No other Aave markets or networks, and no other protocols.</li>
<li class="mb-3 break-inside-avoid leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">The dashboard lists an Aave V4 Spoke only when the wallet has a position or a saved alert in it, and shows no supply APY for V4 positions.</li>
<li class="mb-3 break-inside-avoid leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">Checks run every 5 minutes, not in real time. A fast drop can liquidate a position between two checks.</li>
<li class="mb-3 break-inside-avoid leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">While you&#x27;re below your threshold, every check sends another message on each channel. There is no snooze, digest or recovery message.</li>
<li class="mb-3 break-inside-avoid leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">One threshold per V3 network or V4 Spoke, for the connected wallet only. No watch-only addresses, price alerts or portfolio-wide alerts.</li>
<li class="mb-3 break-inside-avoid leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">Payment is in USDC on Arbitrum One only: no card payments, and the contract has no refund function.</li>
<li class="mb-3 break-inside-avoid leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">Emails have no unsubscribe link yet, and deleting an alert needs active access.</li>
<li class="mb-3 break-inside-avoid leading-relaxed md:leading-[1.75]">Tokenping is in beta. Delivery depends on third-party services, and there is no uptime guarantee.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>
